{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1567691012,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUyODM3MTMyMg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3651#issuecomment-528371322"},"message":"\u003e * Full report on dataset content (related to `status` and its low-level helpers)\n\nIt sounds like their starting point was GitRepo.get_files(), so I suspect GitRepo.get_content_info() would have been an improvement for them.  They landed on a similar `ls-tree, cat-file --batch` design.  Perhaps the processing approaches or just Runner overhead results in get_content_info() being noticeably slower, so as you suggest a benchmark would be very useful.\n\n\u003e * \"is dataset clean\" check (again related to `status`)\n\nI might be missing some other spot where they use a custom is dirty check, but AFAICT [they use our GitRepo.is_dirty()][0].  In that case they [shouldn't see a slowdown][1] when switching the current .dirty that was introduced in 9d29d13bc (OPT: gitrepo.dirty: Use 'git status --porcelain', 2019-05-26).\n\n[0]: https://github.com/OpenNeuroOrg/datalad-service/blob/c9c8d8e970b168755f7b979b4bd4f1c07b8cc2b4/datalad_service/tasks/draft.py#L6-L9\n[1]: https://github.com/datalad/datalad/pull/3460#discussion_r288778925","files":null}]}